+- **A gate starts on a fresh binary and a clone (experiment).** After any cherry-pick or merge that changes `src/` is integrated into main, the facilitator builds the CLI project (`dotnet build src/Avowry.Cli`) before the baseline or final gate, because the Acceptance suite refuses a stale CLI by design. A full gate or sign-off run of a check that needs history (the holdout tests) is made in a single-branch clone of main, not in a `git archive` copy, which has no `.git`; a gate or sign-off brief names both steps, and says that a SHIP rests on facilitator-run evidence where the reviewer could not run `dotnet`.
+  - Hypothesis: the two steps in the brief remove false gate failures that cost a rerun. Metric: gate or sign-off runs failed by a stale binary or a missing `.git`, per gated card (card 324: 2 of 3 runs: 63 Acceptance failures at the baseline gate, 3 holdout failures in the sign-off), target 0. Counter-metric: added gate minutes (a CLI build is about 3 seconds; a clone adds minutes) and any failure that a clone hides. Trial: the next 3 gated cards that change `src/`. Decider D208, started 2026-11-07.
