+- **Dimensions of Difficulty at Ready (experiment; product owner proposal 2026-11-07, adopted with changes).** At the Ready step every card is scored 0, 1 or 2 on four dimensions: Environment (the machine, tooling, runtimes, CI, quotas or access the work depends on), Scope (more than one concern, or more than the slice limits), Unknown (questions the team cannot answer yet) and Communication (someone whose input is needed is not in the loop). Anchors: 0 means assessed and none found (the record says what was checked); 1 means one named, bounded item the card resolves inside its own slice with no one outside the task force; 2 means an item that blocks the card or needs a party outside the task force. Record: one line in the card's issue body and in the committed task-force proposal (`.mob/records/<card>/taskforce-proposal-pm.md`, so a `git show` prints it), `Difficulty: Environment=n Scope=n Unknown=n Communication=n`, with each non-zero item named and, for a 1, how the slice resolves it. Only a 2 fires the prescription, before the card is pulled: Environment escalates to whoever manages it (the product owner for machine actions) and no cycles are spent working around it; Scope splits vertically along the acceptance criteria, never by layer; Unknown creates a spike under the spike rule; Communication becomes more synchronous (a seat at the task force, a question at each boundary, or an inbox question to the product owner). Ready check: the D158 pre-vote checklist for the task-force window has one line that fails the window when the Difficulty line is absent, or when a 2 names no spike, split, inbox entry or seat. A card scoring 0 on all four may use a reduced seat set that the declaration names; the independent gate reviewer and the fresh sign-off stay. The retro reports the four scores against the card's actual flow, and a 0 that the flow contradicts is reported.
+  - Hypothesis: scoring at Ready surfaces the blocking item before the card is pulled, so fewer cycles are spent on environment, scope, unknowns or missing people. Metric: cards where the retro finds a blocker the Ready scores did not name, per card (card 324 was not scored; recent blockers: card 303 environment, the card 266 split scope), target 0. Counter-metric: Ready minutes for the scoring (target under 10) and cards given a prescription for a 2 that resolved without it. Trial: the next 3 cards. Decider D208, started 2026-11-07; enters the mob-defaults template only if the trial succeeds.
